[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/banner.jpg[/img]

Tanks, pipes, pumps and running water for [b]Build 42[/b]. Store water, propane and petrol, pipe them where you need them, and bring a whole house's taps back to life after the water shuts off.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Built for it, server is the authority. Not yet tested on a dedicated server, reports welcome[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Works with[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Power[/b], Dazed Dank, Dazed Butchery[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedPlumbing[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/h-tanks.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/tanks.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]18 tanks[/b]: small, large and extra-large, for water, propane or petrol, in a [b]Salvaged[/b] tier (found or rigged from scrap) and a welded [b]Crafted[/b] tier.
[*]Pour in, take out into bottles and cans, and patch leaks. Damaged tanks leak, even while you are away.
[*]Propane and petrol tanks explode and burn if fire gets too close.
[*]Open-topped tanks catch rain. A gauge window shows level, quality and what feeds and draws from each tank.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/h-pipes.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/pipes.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Right-click a machine, choose its line, and [b]Pipe to[/b] a tank. Runs that meet join automatically, so one line can feed many machines and tanks.
[*][b]Colour-coded and never mixed[/b]: water blue, propane white, petrol red.
[*][b]Shut-off valves[/b] close any line. Pipes are built from pipe sections and need Welding.
[*]Indoors they run overhead, outdoors on the ground. Outdoor pipes wear under zombies and vehicles and need mending.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/h-water.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/water.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Water main[/b]: stand it outside a house, pick the building, and every sink, bath, shower, toilet and washer inside runs from your tank once the town water is off.
[*][b]Taps[/b] pipe a single fixture straight to a tank.
[*][b]Hand and electric water pumps[/b] draw ground water. A [b]drilled well[/b] pumps about 15 L of clean water a minute on Dazed Power.
[*][b]Purifier[/b] cleans dirty water on its way into a tank.
[*][b]Rain collection[/b]: barrels beside a building catch its roof, [b]downspouts[/b] feed a tank from the whole roof, and vanilla rain barrels can be piped in.
[*][b]Garden sprinklers[/b] water crops within 3 squares, with a schedule (dawn, evening, night) and skip-when-raining.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/h-fuel.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/fuel.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Fuel pump[/b]: refuel a parked car or fill petrol cans from a piped petrol tank. Hand-cranked, or electric with Dazed Power.
[*][b]Biogas digester[/b]: feed it rotten food and manure and it slowly makes propane. Slower in the cold, stops below freezing.
[*][b]Smoker[/b]: a propane-fired box that smokes raw meat and fish so it keeps six times longer. Works with Dazed Butchery cuts.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/h-works.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Dazed Power[/b]: propane and petrol generators burn straight from a tank on their line, steam engines are kept topped up with water, and electric pumps, the purifier, the drilled well and the electric fuel pump run off your controller.
[*][b]Dazed Dank[/b]: pipe a hydro reservoir to a water tank to fill and top it up.
[*][b]Dazed Climate[/b] (coming soon): pipes and tanks freeze, and a tank that freezes too full can crack.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/h-sandbox.png[/img]
Water main reach and flow rate, and whether pipe work needs a pipe wrench. Or pick one [b]preset[/b] (Easy, Standard, Realistic, Hardcore) on the Dazed Core page to set every Dazed mod at once.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/h-compat.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only.
[*]Safe to add to an existing save.
[*]Vanilla generators cannot be piped; use Dazed Power's generators.
[*]Art is placeholder for now and will be replaced.
[*]Multiplayer is written for a dedicated server but has not been tested on one yet. If something desyncs, please tell me.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing-Workshop/main/images/h-help.png[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab or open an issue on [url=https://github.com/Dazedgenie/DazedPlumbing]GitHub[/url]. Include your game version, the Dazed mods you run, and your console.txt if there is an error.

